# DogApp — General Rules

## Project structure

- **src/frontend** — frontend (npm, dev: `npm run dev`)
- **src/backend/Dog** — .NET backend: Gateway, services (Identity, Dog), APIs
- **scripts/** — image build and publish; run from `scripts/`
- **deploy/** — Docker Swarm: `docker-compose.*.yml`, deploy scripts

## Enviroments
- Local - to run locally
- Development - to run locally from Docker Swarm
- Stage - to run on stage server, not locally (pre-prod enviroment)

## Communication

- Reply in the same language the user used (English or otherwise).
- In code: comments and names follow repository context (either language is fine).
- Do not comment on code unnecessarily or if it is obvious from the code.

## Before making changes

- Do not duplicate existing logic; check `src/` and `deploy/` before suggesting changes.
- Backend build: from `scripts/` — `./build_backend.sh`; full build — `./build_all.sh`.
- Deploy: from `deploy/` — `./start_local.sh`

## References

- Quick Start and port mappings — see `README.md`.
- Gateway switch (Docker / local) — see `deploy/GATEWAY-SWITCH-MODE.md` (if present).
